{"name":"Mineral Green","hex":"#506355","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mineral green","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A green carbonate of copper; malachite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mineral_green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Basic copper carbonate","blocks":[{"text":"Basic copper carbonate is a chemical compound, more properly called copper(II) carbonate hydroxide. It can be classified as a coordination polymer or a salt. It consists of copper(II) bonded to carbonate and hydroxide with formula Cu2(CO3)(OH)2. It is a green solid that occurs in nature as the mineral malachite. It has been used since antiquity as a pigment, and it is still used as such in artist paints, sometimes called verditer, green bice, or mountain green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Copper_carbonate_basic.jpg/330px-Copper_carbonate_basic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basic_copper_carbonate","wikidata":"Q3792005"},{"title":"Mineral","blocks":[{"text":"In geology and mineralogy, a mineral or mineral species is, broadly speaking, a solid substance with a fairly well-defined chemical composition and a specific crystal structure that occurs naturally in pure form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/S%C3%A9randite%2C_natrolite%2C_analcime%2C_aegirine_300-4-2112.JPG/330px-S%C3%A9randite%2C_natrolite%2C_analcime%2C_aegirine_300-4-2112.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral","wikidata":"Q7946"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Malachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png/500px-Malachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Malachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png/1280px-Malachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Malachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png/500px-Malachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalachite-formula-unit-and-coordination-fade-25-from-xtal-3D-bs-17-25.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Ch%C3%A2teau_Fron